NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS → SUPPORTED; others NOT used per hint.\n- Room table candidates: FCLT_ROOMS (hint-anchored, joins via MEET_PLACE) vs FAC_ROOMS (FAC_* keys, no MEET_PLACE link) vs SPACE_DETAIL (space-assignment perspective, square footage) → only FCLT_ROOMS SUPPORTS the MEET_PLACE join.\n- Department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME is the canonical column (not DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME or *_BK variants) per the hint mapping.\n\n### 4. Business Usage (precedents)\n- **dw_3356 / dw_4527**: exact precedent shape — `STDDEV(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` from TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT on OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE, grouped per department, with no term filter on TIP.\n- **dw_4061**: exact precedent for room stats — `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE = FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY` with AVG/VARIANCE of AREA and an area threshold filter (`r.AREA > 40` there; `> 100` here).\n- **dw_1049**: precedent for the \"departments with more than N subjects offered\" HAVING pattern on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED grouped by department.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n- Filter departments: `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED WHERE TERM_CODE='2022FA' GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_CODE HAVING COUNT(*) > 10`.\n- Physics: `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME='Physics' AND DEPARTMENT_CODE='8'` (dw_1833 precedent uses both name and code).\n- Enrollment stddev: over all TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED rows of the department (precedent dw_3356/dw_4527 apply no term filter).\n- Room stats: catalog subjects of the department joined via MEET_PLACE to FCLT_ROOMS with `AREA > 100` (no term restriction — the 2022FA scope in the question attaches only to the department-selection clause).\n- SELECT exactly 5 columns in asked order: department name, enrollment stddev, avg area, area variance, area stddev; bare STDDEV() per the tip.\n\n",
